{# =========================================================================
   Warp example — flash notices partial
   =========================================================================
   Renders Warp's controller flashes: a success notice (setSuccessFlash) and an
   error notice (setFailFlash). Every Warp auth action that redirects a browser
   sets one of these, so include this near the top of any page a Warp flow can
   land on (login, link-sent, otp-verify, account pages).

   Copy this into your project's templates/ and restyle. The class hooks are
   low-specificity "warp-" names carrying no framework styling; make them yours.

   Accessibility:
   - The error uses role="alert" (assertive) so a screen reader announces it at
     once; the success uses role="status" (polite).
   - On load the error is focused so a keyboard or screen-reader user is taken
     straight to what failed. State is never color-only: each notice carries a
     text label.

   Usage:
     {% include '_partials/flashes' only %}
   ========================================================================= #}

{%- set notice = craft.app.session.getFlash('notice') -%}
{%- set error = craft.app.session.getFlash('error') -%}

{%- if error -%}
    <div class="warp-flash warp-flash--error" role="alert" id="warp-flash-error" tabindex="-1">
        <span class="warp-flash__label">{{ 'Error'|t('warp') }}:</span>
        <span class="warp-flash__message">{{ error }}</span>
    </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if notice -%}
    <div class="warp-flash warp-flash--notice" role="status">
        <span class="warp-flash__label">{{ 'Notice'|t('warp') }}:</span>
        <span class="warp-flash__message">{{ notice }}</span>
    </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if error -%}
    <script>
        (function () {
            var flash = document.getElementById('warp-flash-error');
            if (flash) {
                flash.focus();
            }
        })();
    </script>
{%- endif -%}
